Negative control for the T3.11 handler spec (AC8.3).

Forcing intercepts THIS module's endpoints and nothing else — the collection, one
address, and the verification send — which is the whole reason the app's brand,
settings, config and session boot still reach staging while a preset is armed.
`MODULE_ROUTES` is the only thing that decides that, so this mutant adds one
catch-all route to it and changes nothing else. Every request the page makes now
matches a handler.

The observable is the HANDLER LIST, not the served body: a foreign request under
the mutant is still performed (the resolver hands it back with `passthrough()`),
so an assertion that only reads the eventual response stays green while the
worker has in fact taken over the whole app. What must go red is that a request
outside the module — `brand/settings`, `config/brand/values`, `self`, the oauth
token — is matched by no handler at all.

Bodies must be injected for this control to say anything: `createForceHandlers`
falls back to the runtime corpus, which is empty while `ESC6` is unruled, and an
empty handler list matches nothing under mutant and original alike. Pass the
committed recordings in (the spec lane may read them lawfully — eslint 8h).

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the T3.11 handler spec — the module-scope case (only this module's own
endpoints are handled).

